Package: dsmr-checkpassword-dovecot
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 dovecot-core (>= 2.4),
 qmail (>= 1.06.3)
Recommends: dsmr-qmail-run (>= 1.0-9),
 dovecot-vpopmail
Description: SMTP-AUTH bridge from qmail-smtpd to dovecot's auth-client
 checkpassword-dovecot is a small DJB-style checkpassword program that
 forwards SMTP-AUTH credentials presented to qmail-smtpd to dovecot's
 auth-client protocol over a Unix socket.  The bridge lets one chained
 dovecot passdb stack — vpopmail SQL, /etc/dovecot/system-passwd, PAM —
 serve as the single source of truth for both IMAP login and SMTP
 submission authentication.
 .
 In the DSMR mail stack qmail-submission's checkpassword program is
 vchkpw, which only knows about vpopmail virtual users.  Curated system
 users (e.g., shell accounts who need to relay through the host's mail
 domain) cannot SMTP-AUTH unless that virtual-only constraint is
 relaxed.  This package replaces vchkpw on the submission service with
 the bridge, while leaving inbound port 25 untouched.
 .
 On install this package:
   - Installs /var/qmail/bin/checkpassword-dovecot
   - Installs /usr/sbin/dsmr-smtpauth, an admin tool with add/del/list/
     passwd/test subcommands for /etc/dovecot/system-passwd
   - Drops a dovecot conf snippet exposing an auth-client listener that
     is readable by the vpopmail UID under which qmail-smtpd runs
   - Reloads dovecot so the new listener appears
   - Cycles qmail-submission so the run script (when paired with
     dsmr-qmail-run >= 1.0-9) picks up the bridge
 .
 An allow-list of system users authorised for SMTP-AUTH is maintained at
 /etc/dovecot/system-passwd via the dsmr-smtpauth(8) tool.  Use credentials
 separate from the users' Unix login passwords.
